{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>On that day … the lame</b> — from Israel, who cannot walk swiftly. And likewise: <b>the cast off</b>." "<b>And whom I have afflicted</b> — to them, for I made her a reproach among the nations."], :book :micah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {0 "Reading הצולעה as 'the lame [one]' (feminine singular), understood collectively of Israel; the second lemma הנדחה ('the cast off [one]') is likewise feminine singular.", 1 "The pronoun referents are ambiguous; rendered hyper-literally — 'to them' (להם) and 'her' (the feminine suffix of שמתיה)."}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Micah -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/daat/olam_hatanah/mefaresh.asp?book=20&perek=1&mefaresh=ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:13:52.467653502Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}